WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.781
Lab 2 runs in a worldwide
or G C C test tenant

2
00:00:03.781 --> 00:00:07.725
with Microsoft Entra I
D P1, never production.

3
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:09.742
Before it enforces anything,

4
00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:14.113
build Module 2's emergency accounts
and confirm one can sign in.

5
00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:18.693
And register a phishing-resistant method
for each test administrator first:

6
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:23.201
Microsoft Learn warns that enabling
the policy first risks locking you out.

7
00:00:23.201 --> 00:00:26.795
Then write your tenant's
map, register a reader app,

8
00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:29.163
plan, and apply twice, report-only.

9
00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:32.136
Watch the report-only
results in the sign-in log,

10
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:35.338
and then enforce the gate
alone, with Allow Enforce.

11
00:00:35.338 --> 00:00:39.587
Don't select C one in PIM in
this lab; Module 4 does that.

12
00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:42.120
The reader needs the
three read permissions,

13
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.612
and the apply adds the two write
permissions, and nothing else.

14
00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:49.150
To back out, set each file
the lab created to disabled,

15
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.112
and the contexts to
unavailable, then apply.

16
00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:56.524
Turning a policy off needs no Allow
Enforce, and nothing is deleted.

17
00:00:56.524 --> 00:00:58.730
The authors haven't run Lab 2.
